<Base title="About" description="The Crux builds simple tools for messy business problems. Its first product is a simple Sales & Pre-Sales CRM.">
  <article class="container">
    <header class="page-head">
      <span class="meta-strip">About</span>
      <h1>The Crux builds simple tools for messy business problems.</h1>
      <p>Businesses usually have the tools they need. They still struggle — because information is scattered, workflows are fragmented, and the important decisions get buried in noise.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>The Crux exists to find the important part — the crux — and turn it into something practical you can use today.</p>
      <h2>Our first product</h2>
      <p>A simple <strong>Sales &amp; Pre-Sales CRM</strong> for small and mid-sized B2B teams. It's built for the businesses that run sales on spreadsheets, WhatsApp and memory — the ones who've outgrown Excel but don't want a six-week Salesforce rollout or a CRM consultant on retainer.</p>
      <p>It does the useful things well: capture leads, work a clear pipeline, hand deals to Pre-Sales <em>with the context attached</em>, track proposals, and never miss a follow-up. That's it. If a feature doesn't help a deal move forward, it doesn't make the cut.</p>
      <h2>The way we build</h2>
      <p>Simple enough to start today. Useful enough to keep using every day. We'd rather ship the ten things a sales team touches every morning than a hundred they'll never open.</p>
      <h2>The writing</h2>
      <p>The Crux started as writing that cuts through the noise — sharp takes and honest, tested reviews. That still lives here, under <a href="/essays/">Essays</a> and <a href="/reviews/">Reviews</a>. Same instinct, now pointed at building tools as well as explaining the world.</p>
      <h2>Who's behind it</h2>
      <p>A small team in India, building in the open. If something here is wrong or could be simpler, <a href="/contact/">tell us</a> — that's the whole point.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:28px"><a href="/signup" class="btn-solid">Start your 30-day free trial →</a></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
